 <office:body>
  <office:text>
   <text:p text:style-name="TitlePage">A Test Book</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1">Introduction</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">This small book exists to test how Pitaka imports a PDF. Its first chapter talks about the colour gradi-<text:line-break/>ent of an evening sky over the hills.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The wheel of saṃsāra turns for as long as craving lasts, so the teachers say, and the path is the way out of it.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1">Methods</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The methods chapter describes how the walk was made. We set out early in the morning, before the sun had risen above the ridge, and walked along the river path towards the old mill.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Along the way we counted the birds that we saw and the trees that had fallen in the winter storms. The count was written down in a small notebook that we carried in a coat pocket.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">At the mill the path turns north and climbs steeply through a wood of beech and oak. The ground there is soft and the roots of the trees cross the path in many places.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Near the top of the hill the wood gives way to open heath, and from there the whole valley can be seen laid out below, with the river winding through the fields and the village roofs catching the light of the morning sun as it rose higher and the mist lifted slowly from the water meadows where the cattle were already grazing in the long wet grass beside the hedges that divide one field from the next and run down in crooked lines towards the river bank where the willows grow thickly and the herons stand waiting in the shallows for the fish that come up with the tide each day in spring.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">After resting on the heath we walked back down by the road.</text:p>
  </office:text>
 </office:body>
